Same trajectory as 02_PEEK_one_reaction, but split into one file per frame:

  bonds.reaxff.0.dump, bonds.reaxff.1000.dump, bonds.reaxff.2000.dump

Validation case for reading multiple files via a glob pattern: the files must be read in
natural order (timesteps 0, 1000, 2000) and give the same result as the single-file example. For the file format see 02_PEEK_one_reaction/README.

Expected result for rxn_bond_cutoff in {0, 1, 2}: exactly 1 reaction at timestep 2000,
formation of the bond 703-719 (identical to 02_PEEK_one_reaction).

Reference output of write_reactions() (rxn_bond_cutoff 1): bonds.reaxff_rxnIDs_reference.dat

Usage:
  from atomigraph import AtomiGraph
  topo = AtomiGraph(infile="examples/03_PEEK_multiple_files/bonds.reaxff.*.dump",
                    atom_type_map="1:C,2:H,3:H,4:O,5:O,6:O,7:O,8:O")
  topo.read()
  topo.find_reactions()
